00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:02,867
It's much easier to keep my distance so it won't matter when they're gone.

251
00:11:02,867 --> 00:11:03,867
Thanks for coming with me today.

252
00:11:03,867 --> 00:11:05,867
Prepare your mind to be blown by an awesome script.

253
00:11:05,867 --> 00:11:06,867
Can't wait.

254
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:09,867
This is kind of weird, but hanging out sort of made me feel like that again.

255
00:11:09,867 --> 00:11:10,867
Like what?

256
00:11:10,867 --> 00:11:11,867
Like what?

257
00:11:11,867 --> 00:11:13,867
You know, friends like we were 10 years ago.

258
00:11:13,867 --> 00:11:14,867
I know what you mean.

259
00:11:14,867 --> 00:11:15,867
Like comfortable.

260
00:11:15,867 --> 00:11:16,867
Like comfortable.

261
00:11:16,867 --> 00:11:18,867
It was familiar but sort of felt like starting over.

262
00:11:18,867 --> 00:11:19,867
Hmm.

263
00:11:19,867 --> 00:11:20,867
Well, good night.

264
00:11:20,867 --> 00:11:21,867
See you tomorrow.

265
00:11:21,867 --> 00:11:23,867
Bye.

266
00:11:24,867 --> 00:11:25,867
I'll see you later.

267
00:11:25,867 --> 00:11:27,867
Bye.

268
00:11:27,867 --> 00:11:28,867
Bye.

269
00:11:28,867 --> 00:11:29,867
Bye.

270
00:11:29,867 --> 00:11:30,867
Bye.

271
00:11:30,867 --> 00:11:31,867
Bye.

272
00:11:31,867 --> 00:11:32,867
Bye.

273
00:11:32,867 --> 00:11:33,867
Bye.

274
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:34,867
Bye.

275
00:11:34,867 --> 00:11:35,867
Bye.

276
00:11:35,867 --> 00:11:36,867
Bye.

277
00:11:36,867 --> 00:11:37,867
Bye.

278
00:11:37,867 --> 00:11:38,867
Bye.

279
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:39,867
Bye.

280
00:11:39,867 --> 00:11:40,867
Bye.

281
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:41,867
Bye.

282
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:42,867
Bye.

283
00:11:42,867 --> 00:11:43,867
Bye.

284
00:11:43,867 --> 00:11:44,867
Bye.

285
00:11:44,867 --> 00:11:45,867
Bye.

286
00:11:45,867 --> 00:11:46,867
Bye.

287
00:11:46,867 --> 00:11:59,207
I bet you jerks thought it couldn't be done.

288
00:12:00,207 --> 00:12:02,327
It's pretty awesome if I say so myself.

289
00:12:02,467 --> 00:12:03,947
I have no doubt you guys will agree.

290
00:12:04,067 --> 00:12:05,087
The hardest part's done.

291
00:12:05,207 --> 00:12:06,167
Now let's start filming.

292
00:12:06,707 --> 00:12:08,327
Um, why are you dressed like that?

293
00:12:10,987 --> 00:12:14,087
How dare you speak to racist feet whatever that was...

294
00:12:14,087 --> 00:12:16,127
Shut up, that is so fast!

295
00:12:16,867 --> 00:12:21,547
Hey, this is pretty good.

296
00:12:21,707 --> 00:12:23,167
The dialogue is so intense.

297
00:12:23,187 --> 00:12:25,607
I can't believe this actually came out of you, Yozara.

298
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:27,067
I'm seriously impressed.

299
00:12:27,147 --> 00:12:28,367
You're like a genius or something.

300
00:12:28,607 --> 00:12:29,907
Do you really like it?

301
00:12:31,407 --> 00:12:32,587
I mean, well, duh.

302
00:12:33,067 --> 00:12:35,047
Rika has decided that this is our script.

303
00:12:35,387 --> 00:12:37,107
Next thing we need to do is cast it.

304
00:12:37,467 --> 00:12:39,487
Actually, the cast is already set.

305
00:12:39,947 --> 00:12:42,147
Obviously, I will play our ingenue, Kuya.

306
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:46,247
Kuya's best friend and transfer student, Herotica, will be played by Kotaka.

307
00:12:46,247 --> 00:12:47,407
Oh, that's cool.

308
00:12:47,667 --> 00:12:52,327
Sana, the bitter, jealous, yet questionably popular girl, will be played by meat, of course.

309
00:12:52,467 --> 00:12:52,607
Huh?

310
00:12:53,427 --> 00:12:58,207
Yukimura will be Nobuyuki, the shy little boy who is secretly in love with Herotica.

311
00:12:58,427 --> 00:12:58,827
Okay.

312
00:12:59,207 --> 00:13:03,027
Then there's Sirika, who's always playing stupid pranks on Kuya for being with Herotica.

313
00:13:03,187 --> 00:13:03,947
Rika plays her.

314
00:13:04,307 --> 00:13:04,627
Huh.

315
00:13:04,627 --> 00:13:07,687
Kuya's annoying little sister, Mari, is going to be Maria.

316
00:13:08,847 --> 00:13:09,207
Rude.

317
00:13:09,527 --> 00:13:11,127
Why does she have to be annoying?

318
00:13:11,347 --> 00:13:12,907
Well, is it perfect or is it perfect?

319
00:13:13,127 --> 00:13:14,127
None of the above.

320
00:13:14,307 --> 00:13:15,487
What's the matter, tits?

321
00:13:15,547 --> 00:13:16,487
You don't like your role?

322
00:13:16,487 --> 00:13:19,327
You gave yourself the lead and you made me the villain?

323
00:13:19,587 --> 00:13:21,607
I didn't cast it until I re-read the script.

324
00:13:21,707 --> 00:13:23,267
I just did what made the most sense.

325
00:13:23,707 --> 00:13:27,347
Sana is the popular one, which means she should be devastatingly good-looking.

326
00:13:27,727 --> 00:13:30,267
As much as I hate saying it, you do fit the description.

327
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:32,367
Her past doesn't make her the villain.

328
00:13:32,487 --> 00:13:34,227
It makes her the more relatable character.

329
00:13:35,087 --> 00:13:37,807
You said you wanted a juicy role, right?

330
00:13:38,307 --> 00:13:40,227
Well, it would be nice to show my range.

331
00:13:40,347 --> 00:13:41,127
Yeah, okay, I'm in.

332
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:42,387
Great.

333
00:13:42,607 --> 00:13:43,687
All roles have been accepted.

334
00:13:43,947 --> 00:13:44,867
Rika has a question.

335
00:13:45,427 --> 00:13:47,667
Yes, Rika, you can wear your hair any way you want.

336
00:13:47,787 --> 00:13:49,227
It's not about hair this time.

337
00:13:49,287 --> 00:13:51,267
If we're casting based on looks and personality,

338
00:13:51,267 --> 00:13:55,327
then Rika has to say that Kotaka as the stud transfer student is not the best choice.

339
00:13:55,587 --> 00:13:55,987
Me?

340
00:13:56,147 --> 00:13:56,767
But why not?

341
00:13:56,767 --> 00:14:00,467
Herotika's personality doesn't seem to work.

342
00:14:00,667 --> 00:14:04,747
He's honorable, he has a passion for justice, he's courageous, he's totally popular.

343
00:14:05,087 --> 00:14:07,627
He's supposed to be funny and sociable and charming, right?

344
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:10,567
You have him written as tall and athletic with rugged features.

345
00:14:11,407 --> 00:14:12,667
It's like we're twins.

346
00:14:13,027 --> 00:14:15,367
Nothing about this guy sounds anything like Kotaka.

347
00:14:15,507 --> 00:14:16,607
No one would ever believe it.

348
00:14:16,827 --> 00:14:18,687
I didn't think it would be that noticeable.

349
00:14:18,947 --> 00:14:20,127
Wait, what's that noticeable?

350
00:14:20,307 --> 00:14:21,487
I was thinking the same thing.

351
00:14:21,547 --> 00:14:23,027
You couldn't do a worse casting job.

352
00:14:23,107 --> 00:14:24,487
The real Herotika would be offended.

353
00:14:24,487 --> 00:14:27,427
If Big Brother wasn't puny, he might look like a cool guy.

354
00:14:28,807 --> 00:14:30,067
Is there another reason?

355
00:14:30,407 --> 00:14:32,927
Why would anyone choose Kotaka as a leading man type?

356
00:14:33,067 --> 00:14:34,027
Yeah, there is actually.

357
00:14:34,947 --> 00:14:36,127
It's not about the look.

358
00:14:36,387 --> 00:14:38,867
It's because Kotaka and I have known each other since we were kids.

359
00:14:40,467 --> 00:14:42,407
That's right, I almost forgot about that.

360
00:14:42,507 --> 00:14:44,207
Kuya and Herotika were childhood friends,

361
00:14:44,267 --> 00:14:47,267
so I chose my actual childhood friend to play opposite me in the film.

362
00:14:47,407 --> 00:14:49,467
I figured it would be more realistic for us both.

363
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:51,067
Is there anything else I can help you with?

364
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:53,367
No, maybe a dressing room with candy?

365
00:14:53,587 --> 00:14:54,587
Let me get this straight.

366
00:14:54,687 --> 00:14:55,687
If you don't play Kuya,

367
00:14:55,787 --> 00:14:58,287
then we don't have to cast your actual friend as the lead, right?

368
00:14:58,407 --> 00:15:00,687
In fact, we may not even need that character at all.

369
00:15:00,767 --> 00:15:02,107
What are you trying to say, Rika?

370
00:15:02,347 --> 00:15:05,267
It's just that maybe we should all vote on the cast instead.

371
00:15:05,647 --> 00:15:06,807
I can get behind that.

372
00:15:07,027 --> 00:15:08,347
Hey, nobody's talking to you.

373
00:15:08,427 --> 00:15:09,187
What's the matter?

374
00:15:09,307 --> 00:15:11,767
Are you worried that we won't vote for you as Kuya or something?

375
00:15:12,867 --> 00:15:13,907
Of course I'm not.

376
00:15:13,987 --> 00:15:15,867
I know you guys want this movie to be good, too.

377
00:15:15,867 --> 00:15:23,227
Okay, all the votes are tallied, and this is what we've got.

378
00:15:25,107 --> 00:15:27,907
If I'm playing Kuya, that means I'm the lead?

379
00:15:29,587 --> 00:15:31,027
This is so ridiculous.

380
00:15:31,447 --> 00:15:31,767
Yay!

381
00:15:32,187 --> 00:15:35,007
I get to be the bitter, bossy, booby, popular pretty girl!

382
00:15:35,987 --> 00:15:37,707
Yep, that is awkward.

383
00:15:38,207 --> 00:15:40,547
No, Luyuki, so Rika's playing a young boy?

384
00:15:40,547 --> 00:15:41,347
What the crap?

385
00:15:42,427 --> 00:15:43,787
You've got to be kidding me!

386
00:15:44,047 --> 00:15:46,807
How did I go from the male lead to playing the little sister?

387
00:15:50,167 --> 00:15:51,687
This is your fault, isn't it?

388
00:15:51,687 --> 00:15:52,867
It's not like I had a choice.

389
00:15:53,207 --> 00:15:54,927
Plus, I thought you might enjoy a challenge.

390
00:15:55,187 --> 00:15:57,287
Well, you're wrong, and what do you mean you didn't have a choice?

391
00:15:57,607 --> 00:15:59,307
Can we discuss why you're yelling at me?

392
00:15:59,367 --> 00:16:00,627
I'm not the only one who voted.

393
00:16:00,967 --> 00:16:02,327
Who else voted for me, then?

394
00:16:02,507 --> 00:16:02,727
Me!

395
00:16:03,167 --> 00:16:04,087
What? Why?

396
00:16:04,707 --> 00:16:06,087
Because it looks like fun!

397
00:16:06,267 --> 00:16:07,507
You're big brother every day.

398
00:16:07,667 --> 00:16:09,387
I wanted to see you be someone different.

399
00:16:09,387 --> 00:16:11,767
Doesn't get any more non-brother than being a sister!

400
00:16:12,687 --> 00:16:16,247
Rika thinks there may have been ulterior motives for voting the way we did.

401
00:16:16,587 --> 00:16:18,727
At least no one can accuse us of typecasting.

402
00:16:18,907 --> 00:16:20,987
Yeah, I don't know that this is what we're going for.

403
00:16:21,367 --> 00:16:22,507
Shouldn't we take another vote?

404
00:16:28,227 --> 00:16:30,287
I mean, it's gonna be fine.

405
00:16:30,687 --> 00:16:32,467
You'll make an amazing lead, Yukimura.

406
00:16:33,247 --> 00:16:33,887
Thank you.

407
00:16:34,107 --> 00:16:35,647
I promise to make you proud, sir.

408
00:16:35,887 --> 00:16:36,787
Of course you will.

409
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:39,087
I just need to figure out how to get into my role.

410
00:16:39,387 --> 00:16:41,667
I guess I'll change it to a little brother.

411
00:16:42,187 --> 00:16:44,267
It's not going to hurt the story if we switch genders.

412
00:16:44,907 --> 00:16:45,667
Now what?

413
00:16:45,767 --> 00:16:47,027
Do you want to play a little boy?

414
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:48,187
Uh, no.

415
00:16:48,887 --> 00:16:50,227
I just kind of feel bad.

416
00:16:50,547 --> 00:16:50,867
Huh?

417
00:16:51,287 --> 00:16:55,047
Well, you wrote the whole script, and I just made even more work for you.

418
00:16:55,107 --> 00:16:55,587
Hold on.

419
00:16:55,667 --> 00:16:58,987
I feel like you're showing signs of having a soul, and it's creeping me out a bit.

420
00:16:59,087 --> 00:17:00,027
Rude.com!

421
00:17:00,027 --> 00:17:03,147
I-I just liked your script, okay?

422
00:17:03,367 --> 00:17:04,267
It's pretty awesome.

423
00:17:04,747 --> 00:17:04,987
Ugh.

424
00:17:05,447 --> 00:17:06,127
Thank you.

425
00:17:06,487 --> 00:17:08,827
I mean, it's not a big deal to change a sister to a brother.

426
00:17:08,947 --> 00:17:10,227
The script's basically the same.

427
00:17:10,307 --> 00:17:11,407
Oh, you sure?

428
00:17:11,867 --> 00:17:13,687
Well, then, I guess it's fine.

429
00:17:13,687 --> 00:17:25,387
What the hell is happening?

430
00:17:26,287 --> 00:17:28,407
This is a completely different story now.

431
00:17:28,487 --> 00:17:28,587
Why?

432
00:17:28,987 --> 00:17:29,687
It's still the same.

433
00:17:29,767 --> 00:17:30,927
Um, no, it is not.

434
00:17:31,087 --> 00:17:32,927
Who the heck is this Kotaro guy?

435
00:17:33,007 --> 00:17:33,827
Kuya's little brother.

436
00:17:34,087 --> 00:17:35,987
I know, but why are they suddenly twins?

437
00:17:36,267 --> 00:17:37,367
Mari was never a twin.

438
00:17:37,527 --> 00:17:38,087
Why now?

439
00:17:38,187 --> 00:17:39,207
What are you trying to pull?

440
00:17:39,327 --> 00:17:40,887
This is not what I signed up for.

441
00:17:41,387 --> 00:17:45,087
A little suspicious how he went from a side character to pretty much the new lead.

442
00:17:45,167 --> 00:17:49,407
This was supposed to be about Kuya and Herodika's friendship, but now you have them hating each other.

443
00:17:49,587 --> 00:17:51,967
Yeah, because they were never that close to begin with.

444
00:17:52,067 --> 00:17:53,507
I just forgot to write it in, okay?

445
00:17:53,687 --> 00:17:55,207
But you said they were best friends.

446
00:17:55,547 --> 00:17:58,607
No, Herodika just thought of Kuya as a friend of a best friend.

447
00:17:58,607 --> 00:18:00,687
He knew her, but that's about as far as it went.

448
00:18:00,687 --> 00:18:05,307
She was actually friends with Kotaro, who was friends with Herodika, so they all hung out together.

449
00:18:05,487 --> 00:18:07,367
That sounds like a lot to keep up with.

450
00:18:07,547 --> 00:18:09,727
What's wrong with letting all three of them be friends?

451
00:18:10,527 --> 00:18:12,947
Because friend of a friend does not mean friend.

452
00:18:13,147 --> 00:18:14,667
It just means acquaintances.

453
00:18:15,007 --> 00:18:15,427
Huh?

454
00:18:15,967 --> 00:18:18,227
Besides, I don't want to write about a three-way friendship.

455
00:18:18,407 --> 00:18:19,067
It's too hard.

456
00:18:19,167 --> 00:18:20,567
It's two friends and their friend.

457
00:18:20,967 --> 00:18:22,827
I guess I kind of understand what you mean.

458
00:18:22,887 --> 00:18:23,887
That doesn't make sense.

459
00:18:23,887 --> 00:18:28,827
Why not keep Kuya and Herodika best friends and make Kotaro the odd one out since he's the new character?

460
00:18:28,827 --> 00:18:30,847
That way you don't have to change the story.

461
00:18:30,967 --> 00:18:31,887
Sorry, it won't work.

462
00:18:32,227 --> 00:18:32,947
Why not?

463
00:18:33,207 --> 00:18:35,747
Because it's much more natural for him to get along with Kotaro.

464
00:18:36,407 --> 00:18:38,627
I mean, since that's who Kotaka's gonna be playing.

465
00:18:40,127 --> 00:18:41,107
I get it now.

466
00:18:41,307 --> 00:18:44,147
You just want Kotaka to play whoever your friend is in the film.

467
00:18:44,987 --> 00:18:46,447
Yeah, it makes sense that way.

468
00:18:47,087 --> 00:18:47,987
No, it doesn't.

469
00:18:48,027 --> 00:18:50,407
You're just recreating the past instead of telling a story.

470
00:18:50,407 --> 00:18:55,227
What did you say to me?

471
00:19:03,707 --> 00:19:06,307
Well, what past am I recreating?

472
00:19:06,627 --> 00:19:09,527
Uh, the past of you and Kotaka being close friends?

473
00:19:09,647 --> 00:19:10,667
That shouldn't matter now.

474
00:19:10,907 --> 00:19:12,987
You should be trying to tell a new original story,

475
00:19:13,067 --> 00:19:15,467
not using this movie as a way to try to turn back time.

476
00:19:15,467 --> 00:19:16,927
How dare you?

477
00:19:17,147 --> 00:19:18,107
That isn't true.

478
00:19:18,287 --> 00:19:19,487
Stop being so dramatic.

479
00:19:19,507 --> 00:19:22,007
You're the only one being dramatic and obsessing about the past.

480
00:19:22,127 --> 00:19:23,787
Quit trying so hard to hold on to it.

481
00:19:23,847 --> 00:19:26,287
You're dragging everyone else down with you and it's not fair.

482
00:19:33,227 --> 00:19:34,267
Yozra, are you okay?

483
00:19:34,427 --> 00:19:35,227
It's your fault.

484
00:19:35,687 --> 00:19:38,167
If you weren't here, I wouldn't have to feel like this.

485
00:19:38,587 --> 00:19:39,527
It's your fault.

486
00:19:39,527 --> 00:19:39,607
It's your fault.

487
00:19:39,607 --> 00:19:44,607
Jerk, you just wait.

488
00:19:45,127 --> 00:19:47,747
Someday you're gonna know exactly how this feels!

489
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:51,787
Yozra, come back!

490
00:19:56,307 --> 00:19:58,087
I didn't mean for that to happen.

491
00:19:58,307 --> 00:19:58,867
I'm sorry.

492
00:20:00,067 --> 00:20:01,147
This sucks.

493
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:02,987
Maybe I shouldn't have been so honest.

494
00:20:03,487 --> 00:20:05,607
I was only trying to get through to her.

495
00:20:06,087 --> 00:20:07,707
Why can't she let the past go?

496
00:20:09,607 --> 00:20:10,447
I'm sorry.

497
00:20:25,447 --> 00:20:25,747
Yozra.

498
00:20:25,887 --> 00:20:26,107
Ah!

499
00:20:26,847 --> 00:20:27,587
What are you doing?

500
00:20:28,007 --> 00:20:28,347
Nothing.

501
00:20:28,487 --> 00:20:30,187
I forgot my bag in gym class today.

502
00:20:30,287 --> 00:20:30,787
That's all.

503
00:20:30,967 --> 00:20:32,027
Sucks when that happens.

504
00:20:32,027 --> 00:20:41,307
What do you think?

505
00:20:41,787 --> 00:20:44,167
Should Herodica be best friends with Kuya or Kotaro?

506
00:20:44,747 --> 00:20:45,507
Be honest.

507
00:20:46,147 --> 00:20:47,627
It makes no difference to me.

508
00:20:47,727 --> 00:20:49,167
I just want the story to be good.

509
00:20:50,147 --> 00:20:50,787
I know.

510
00:20:51,247 --> 00:20:52,027
I just...

511
00:20:52,027 --> 00:20:53,447
I want it to be you.

512
00:20:53,807 --> 00:20:54,087
Huh?

513
00:20:54,447 --> 00:20:55,547
I didn't quite catch that.

514
00:20:55,987 --> 00:20:57,547
Tell me which is more important to you.

515
00:20:57,647 --> 00:21:00,227
Our friendship the way it was ten years ago or the way it is now.

516
00:21:00,227 --> 00:21:01,787
I don't know how to answer that.

517
00:21:01,847 --> 00:21:02,607
They're both different.

518
00:21:02,727 --> 00:21:05,087
If they're so different, then you should have a preference, right?

519
00:21:05,107 --> 00:21:06,327
I guess I need inspiration.

520
00:21:06,527 --> 00:21:07,227
What's your pick?

521
00:21:08,107 --> 00:21:11,527
Would you go back to ten years ago or are you happy with the way things are?

522
00:21:11,807 --> 00:21:13,747
Um, well, that's a no-brainer for me.

523
00:21:13,867 --> 00:21:14,927
I'd go back ten years.

524
00:21:15,047 --> 00:21:16,967
Does that mean the present isn't as important?

525
00:21:17,347 --> 00:21:17,767
Uh-huh.

526
00:21:21,687 --> 00:21:22,827
It's hard to explain.

527
00:21:23,747 --> 00:21:24,787
I know what you mean.

528
00:21:25,647 --> 00:21:26,007
Yeah.

529
00:21:26,007 --> 00:21:26,067
Yeah.

530
00:21:26,067 --> 00:21:26,107
Yeah.

531
00:21:26,107 --> 00:21:26,147
Yeah.

532
00:21:30,227 --> 00:21:35,607
My toads love it.

533
00:21:36,607 --> 00:21:39,747
You really shouldn't be shocked for my ability to make adjustments.

534
00:21:40,047 --> 00:21:41,667
Rika is so excited and relieved.

535
00:21:41,787 --> 00:21:44,527
This story is ten thousand times better than the last one you wrote.

536
00:21:44,627 --> 00:21:45,247
Good job.

537
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:47,207
Rika was worried you were going to change Kotaro.

538
00:21:47,627 --> 00:21:48,727
Thank goodness you didn't.

539
00:21:48,867 --> 00:21:49,987
It's perfect this way.

540
00:21:50,087 --> 00:21:51,947
It's obvious you worked very hard on this.

541
00:21:52,047 --> 00:21:52,527
Thank you.

542
00:21:52,727 --> 00:21:53,987
Thank you for your feedback.

543
00:21:53,987 --> 00:21:58,847
Okay, well, if no one else has any other questions, I say we get moving.

544
00:21:59,047 --> 00:22:00,367
I'm ready to film this thing.

545
00:22:00,447 --> 00:22:01,187
How about you?

546
00:22:01,227 --> 00:22:01,867
We're going to rule.

547
00:22:01,887 --> 00:22:03,207
I hope I do your story justice.

548
00:22:03,207 --> 00:22:05,907
This movie has no choice but to be the best because I'm in it.

549
00:22:06,047 --> 00:22:07,087
Shut up, Titzilla.

550
00:22:07,467 --> 00:22:10,207
This story sounds familiar for some reason.

551
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:44,460
Dear Mademoiselle Yozora, you look so very sad and alone over there.

552
00:23:44,460 --> 00:23:48,460
Oh, sing. I was happy that she was able to explore and learn more about her love story.

553
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:51,460
We hope we helped, but fair is fair, my sweet.

554
00:23:51,460 --> 00:23:54,460
Next time, share the secrets of your heart or bedroom.

555
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:57,460
Now to sleep, my Stephanie. Je t'aime always.

556
00:23:57,460 --> 00:23:59,460
Oh, dear Jonathan, a million times, je t'aime.

557
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:03,460
Please join us next time for Stray Cats Overheat.

558
00:24:03,460 --> 00:24:06,460
Wait just a minute. My loins are overheating!

559
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:09,460
Oh, c'est bon! C'est bon!

560
00:24:10,460 --> 00:24:11,460
Thank you.

